# Confronted by an enemy: they must be looked at like anything else, and the rest of the room is
# still there.
#
# The wolf in the Test Den confronts whoever walks in. Two things used to follow that no longer do:
#
#  - the wolf stood on the trees already observed, so it could be thought about without a look, the
#    one case in the game where a thought came before an observation. It is now the hostile symbol
#    on the card until a mind observes it, for a point, as anything is;
#  - nothing but the wolf could be looked at or thought about. A confrontation now holds the member
#    where they stand and no more: what is in their own area answers, what is elsewhere does not.
#    What may be DONE is the rules' business — the rules of choice offer only the acts that answer
#    the confronter unless a discreet means is held (this kit holds two), and the rules of action
#    refuse on the click a means that is not discreet.
#
# FLAGS: --playground --skip-childhood --debug --seed 42 --no-encounters --location-type test --location-id 0 --npc-static --start-area "Test Den" --period noon

wait
click menu New
wait mode ProtagonistCreation 20
click continue
wait mode WorldView 60
travel here
wait mode LocationInteraction 60
advance 12 180

# Confronted on arrival, and nothing observed: the wolf is a symbol, not a tree.
expect-state where confronted=Enemy:wolf exit=RUNAWAY

# The screen and the music say so: the card is framed (the frame's glyphs stand, only their ink
# beats), and the music is asked for the place's standoff.
expect ╔═
expect ╚
expect-state music confronted=yes
expect-no-state trees wolf
inspect symbols
expect-state symbols click observe hostile in Test Den x1
expect-no-state symbols click observe hostile in Test Den x1 (disabled)

# The way out of the den is in my own area: it answers. What stands in another area does not, and
# no card can be walked to.
expect-state symbols click observe the way to Test Wood in Test Den (way)
expect-no-state symbols click observe the way to Test Wood in Test Den (way) (disabled)
expect-state symbols click observe thing in Test Wood x1 (disabled)
click area "Test Wood"
expect-state where area=Test Den

# Something other than the wolf is looked at, and thought about: a discreet means is held, so the
# acts it affords are still offered.
click observe "Test Wood"
choose childhood_memory
advance 12 180
expect-state trees element "the way to Test Wood" kind=way
expect-state symbols click think the way to Test Wood
expect-no-state symbols click think the way to Test Wood (disabled)

# The wolf, now: a look first, then the thought.
click observe hostile
choose childhood_memory
advance 12 180
expect-state trees wolf
strategy succeed
goal appease
click think "wolf"
choose ripelore
advance 12 180
expect-state trees act state=waiting verb=appease
quit
